WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.369 --> 00:00:04.100
Throughout the movie, there are these foreign
words that appear on walls and are never really

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.100
explained.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.840
So, if you want to hear all about the meanings
of the symbology and phrases hidden around

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:16.120
the film, stick around to the end of this
video.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.950
As with all Things You Missed episodes, there
will be spoilers, I just wanted to emphasize

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.020
this time because film goes to some really
unexpected places, so do yourself the favor

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:26.640
of watching the movie before you watch this
video.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.060
So with that being said, wow!

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.240
This was a crazy movie!

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.539
I did not expect this to become a possession
film, but looking back on it, the signs are

00:00:34.539 --> 00:00:35.539
all there.

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:39.239
I even noticed a lot of the signs, like the
necklace and decapitated figures when I did

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:43.089
the Things You Missed on the trailer way back
in January, but they withheld enough information

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:45.140
to keep us in the dark during the movie.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.570
So let's start at the beginning.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.510
The very first thing we see is a title card
letting us know about the passing of the grandmother,

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.510
Ellen.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.609
And it also introduces us to her daughter,
Annie and her granddaughter, Charlie.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:58.739
The three generations of women are the basis
for this movie’s title, Hereditary, or something

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:02.520
determined by genetic factors and therefore
able to be passed on from parents to their

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.030
offspring or descendants.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.440
What is this trait being passed down?

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.130
We don't find that out until later.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.570
The first shot we see is the treehouse, little
do we know it's actually a chapel of demonic

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.570
worship.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:13.570
Hear that?

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.750
That's the sound of exploding heads from everyone
who didn't take my advice to just see the

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.750
movie first.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.730
This treehouse is significant because at the
beginning of the film, the family is getting

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:24.420
ready to head to the grandmother's funeral
service and they can't find Charlie, because

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.740
she actually sleeps out in the treehouse.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:30.090
When the Mom finds her there, she's upset
because it's apparently it's really cold and

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.200
she's worried that Charlie might catch pneumonia,
to which Charlie says, “I don't care.”

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.130
Getting pneumonia is pretty serious, unless
you're planning on ditching your current vessel

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.280
for a new body some time soon.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.600
Based off of that, the demon, King Paimon,
is already in possession of the Charlie's

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:47.200
body at the start of the movie; possibly before
she's even born.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.460
Her mother tells her she never once cried
as a baby and that the Grandmother really

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.890
wanted her to be a boy, suggesting that she
had been planning to make the child into a

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:58.280
male vessel befitting the demon from before
Charlie’s birth.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:02.660
The doormat embroidered by the Grandma even
says ‘Charles’ instead of Charlie.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.250
At the funeral, Annie gives quite a strange
eulogy for her mother.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.250
Let's roll it.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.180
“It’s heartening to see so many strange
new faces here today.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:17.340
I know my Mom would be very touched, and probably
a little suspicious.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.459
My mother was a very secretive and private
woman.

00:02:19.459 --> 00:02:20.459
She had private rituals.

00:02:20.459 --> 00:02:21.459
Private friends.

00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:22.459
”

00:02:22.459 --> 00:02:26.900
I think it’s pretty clear what those ‘private
rituals’ are now, knowing that she was the

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:30.849
leader, or as they call it in the movie, Queen,
of a demonic cult.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:33.420
As for the private friends she mentioned,
they are her followers.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.700
She notes that the faces who show up to the
funeral are not familiar, and that is probably

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.700
why.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:41.760
In fact, I think the naked people who appear
in the house toward the end of the movie

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.979
(A24 loves their creepy naked old people don’t
they?)

00:02:44.979 --> 00:02:48.079
.. are probably some of the same people who
show up at the service, though I would have

00:02:48.079 --> 00:02:51.360
no way of confirming this until I have a copy
of the movie, so don’t chop my head off

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.950
if that doesn’t end up being true.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.599
Also, if anyone can find Joan in the crowd
somewhere, then tweet me a picture of it,

00:02:56.599 --> 00:02:57.599
yeah?

00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:01.209
I believe it was as they are leaving the funeral,
when we see Charlie eating a chocolate bar,

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:03.010
and chocolate can associated with the devil.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:04.010
It’s the devil’s temptation.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.819
That’s why you have devil’s food cake,
which is the chocolate one and angel’s food

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:09.709
cake which is the… not chocolate one.

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:13.950
I’m pretty sure chocolate is the only thing
we see her eat, first this the chocolate bar,

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:16.450
and second, the chocolate cake at the party.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.840
Side note: I absolutely love how she eats
the chocolate exactly like Mello from Death

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.280
Note.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.749
I was smiling to myself in the theater when
I saw that.

00:03:25.749 --> 00:03:29.249
I also dug the red doorknob, I think it was
on Peter’s room, or possibly Charlie’s,

00:03:29.249 --> 00:03:31.069
and that’s a reference to The Sixth Sense.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:34.370
It could also be that the red doorknob was
used in a similar way, to indicate the presence

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:38.599
of spirits, so I found that to be an interesting
parallel, because the two films share a lot

00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:39.599
of similarities.

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:43.290
So the family gets home from the funeral and
they’re all dealing with grief in their

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.290
own ways.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.120
Annie recreates moments from of her Mother’s
life using her miniatures.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.569
So what’s the meaning behind the miniatures?

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:49.569
Here’s my interpretation.

00:03:49.569 --> 00:03:54.560
It has to do with one of the traits that is
passed down in the family, manipulation.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.049
Starting at the top, King Paimon manipulates
Ellen into leading the cult that worships

00:03:58.049 --> 00:04:00.549
him by offering to make her his Queen.

00:04:00.549 --> 00:04:03.239
In turn, Ellen manipulates the entire family.

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:07.970
Annie, Steve, Charlie and Peter, are all her
pawns in her plot to resurrect King Paimon.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:12.480
She’s orchestrating all the pieces that
lead to King Paimon getting into his intended

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.090
body, Peter’s body.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.280
Annie is subconsciously at King Paimon’s
will as well, but her mind is strong enough

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.209
to resist him, at least for the time being.

00:04:19.209 --> 00:04:22.560
This is why he’s only able to control her
subconscious, the reason she finds herself

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.120
on the verge of burning up her son while sleepwalking,
and the reason she finds herself creating

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.669
miniature versions of the tragic events that
lead up to the body transfer.

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:33.180
Her manipulation of the miniature figures
represents her Mother’s manipulation of

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.220
the actual household.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:38.629
But it doesn’t stop there, because Charlie
is also into arts and crafts, making her own

00:04:38.629 --> 00:04:42.949
miniature figures and idols, and eventually
making the life sized King Paimon idol that

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.919
we see that the end of the movie.

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:48.139
She doesn’t seem to have any other interests
outside of creating these demented figures.

00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:52.410
She’s doing sketches at the funeral, modifying
some toy during class and cutting up a dead

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.790
bird at recess.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.430
So this manipulation is a trait that runs
all the way down the family line, and seems

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.940
to be passed to all the females.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:03.060
I also did a little reading on King Paimon,
and apparently he has a flare for the arts,

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.840
and people like to call on him to assist their
creative projects, which is why Annie and

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.530
Charlie display their traits through their
craft.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.300
As we get later into the movie Annie’s mind
is gets weaker and weaker, Annie works less

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:17.570
on the model for her work, and more on personal
pieces representing the family, because she’ll

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.539
soon be a pawn of King Paimon like her mother
before her.

00:05:20.539 --> 00:05:24.370
As Peter’s classmate put it in a discussion
about the flaws of Greek mythological figure

00:05:24.370 --> 00:05:28.509
Heracles, “The characters are all just pawns
in this horrible hopelessness.”

00:05:28.509 --> 00:05:31.389
I think that stands for the movie, Hereditary
as well.

00:05:31.389 --> 00:05:34.860
Ellen obviously doesn’t see it that way
though, because she leaves a note for Annie,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.560
essentially apologizing for what’s happened
so far and what’s about to happen, but saying

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:42.240
that these sacrifices must be made and everything
will be good in the end.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.940
I’m paraphrasing here, but she’s basically
outlining her plan to tear apart the family

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:49.680
with tragedy, so that she can become the queen
and they can join the cult of Paimon.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.340
This begins before her death.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.630
At the first group meeting that Annie goes
to to try to ease her grief, she talks a little

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:58.729
bit about her family history and mentions
that her Mom has DID and dementia.

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:02.460
DID, if you don’t know, is short for dissociative
identity disorder, commonly referred to as

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.879
multiple personality disorder.

00:06:03.879 --> 00:06:06.771
I don’t think she really had this disorder
though.

00:06:06.771 --> 00:06:10.240
It would make a lot of sense if she was starting
to lose control to King Paimon making it appear

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.669
that she was switching personalities.

00:06:11.669 --> 00:06:15.220
If that’s the case it could also help explain
her dementia.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:18.210
Not much background is given on the rest of
the family, but we know that Annie’s father

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:22.099
starved himself and her brother commited suicide,
which brings me to the second trait that is

00:06:22.099 --> 00:06:26.180
passed down in Hereditary, though it’s not
so much a trait as it is a commonality, that

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.169
they all suffer tragic deaths.

00:06:28.169 --> 00:06:32.090
You have to believe that King Paimon is somehow
involved in carrying that out.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.229
That all comes to a head with Charlie.

00:06:34.229 --> 00:06:38.039
At 13, she should be old enough to check anything
she eats in regards to her food allergy, but

00:06:38.039 --> 00:06:41.810
something causes her to eat that cake anyway,
and just when it looks like Peter might be

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:45.560
able to rush her to the hospital in time,
she sticks her head out the window and gets

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:48.039
decapitated by the pole on the side of the
road.

00:06:48.039 --> 00:06:53.030
But this no accident, it’s all part of Ellen
and King Paimon’s plan.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.250
Decapitation seems to somehow be a requirement
for the cult, because we see the same thing

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.840
happen to the bodies of Ellen and Annie.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:02.770
If you need any further proof, the symbol
of King Paimon can be seen on that same pole

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.020
as Peter and Charlie head to party.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.120
Nearly everything that the demon has manipulated
has this symbol.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:12.129
It’s on Annie and Ellen’s necklaces, in
Joan’s house after she’s placed the curse

00:07:12.129 --> 00:07:16.909
on Annie, and written in blood on the roof
of the attic where Ellen’s body is stored.

00:07:16.909 --> 00:07:20.409
When we see the King at the end the idol also
wears that symbol.

00:07:20.409 --> 00:07:25.270
I already mentioned how one of Peter’s classmates
has the on point Heracles analysis, well in

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:28.569
another class he’s learning about the Great
Depression, you can see it written on the

00:07:28.569 --> 00:07:32.600
chalkboard, and how it was started by the
Great Crash, which was when the stock market

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.639
crashed in 1929.

00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:38.110
You could say the same about the family in
the movie though, that a great depression

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:41.080
was cast over them after a great crash.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:44.479
After that depression sets in, the demon,
with the help of Ellen’s ‘secret’ friend

00:07:44.479 --> 00:07:48.610
Joan, starts to take over the family in order
to get the the body he wants.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:52.550
Joan pretends to befriend Annie at the support
group so that she can ease her into the idea

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:55.150
of performing the ritual to summon King Paimon.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:59.050
She is almost given away by her doormat, which
was made by Annie’s mother who embroidered

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:03.900
the doormats for the grandkids, but Annie
ends up brushing it off as just a similar

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.900
style.

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:07.580
Eventually, Annie does find out that Joan
and Ellen were in cahoots, all she had to

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.900
do was look in her mother’s left behind
photo album, but their relationship was so

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:14.159
bad that Ellen didn’t even have to worry
about her daughter finding out.

00:08:14.159 --> 00:08:17.901
In fact, it’s mentioned that they were practically
estranged until the birth of Charlie, when

00:08:17.901 --> 00:08:22.870
Ellen suddenly started to take interest, for
obvious reasons: she had plans for Charlie.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:26.370
Suddenly, all the weird stuff from early on
starts to make more sense.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.540
How Charlie was her Grandmother’s favorite
child.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:32.789
How Annie kept Ellen away from Peter but,
quote, “Gave Charlie to her.”

00:08:32.789 --> 00:08:35.440
How Annie wasn’t even allowed to breastfeed
her daughter, “because she needed to feed

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.440
you.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.440
Because she needed to feed you.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.440
Because she needed to feed you.”

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:41.470
And how Charlie wondered who would be taking
care of her now that Ellen was gone.

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:45.160
But as Annie starts to figure out what’s
going on, she begins to lose herself to the

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:47.019
fate destined by her DNA.

00:08:47.019 --> 00:08:50.709
All the sudden she can only get to sleep in
the treehouse, which, as a reminder, is a

00:08:50.709 --> 00:08:53.040
freezing cold demon worship site.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:54.860
Fights break out at the dinner table.

00:08:54.860 --> 00:08:58.720
Annie accuses Peter of looking at her with
that face on his face,

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.740
All I do is worry,

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:03.380
and all I get back is that face on your face!

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:04.560
possible reference

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.200
to the fact that he is not destined to possess
his own body.

00:09:08.209 --> 00:09:11.950
Also after the death of Charlie, we start
to see this light flare occasionally come

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:12.950
up.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.260
I believe this strange light is the physical
manifestation of King Paimon when he is not

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.670
inside of a body.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:21.540
We see it stalk Peter in the hall at school,
where he ends up temporarily losing himself

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:23.990
to King Paimon and smashing his face against
the desk.

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:27.881
Then it comes up after the father, Steve,
bursts into flames, suggesting that it’s

00:09:27.881 --> 00:09:29.750
traveling from body to body.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:33.880
Then near the end, when Peter commits suicide
by jumping out the window, the light travels,

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.860
lands on him, then disappears.

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:38.540
When Peter’s body reawakes, he is taken
over by King Paimon.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:43.320
He goes to his new place of worship, the treehouse,
where the movie ends with many voices chanting

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.089
the name of the king of Hell.

00:09:45.089 --> 00:09:48.940
There are only like 6 or so people in the
tree house, and half of them are beheaded,

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:53.029
but it sounds like 20 or more voices chanting,
which created a creepy effect that actually

00:09:53.029 --> 00:09:55.810
sounded like the audience members in front
of me were chanting too.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.920
So that covers everything that I noticed in
the movie except for the strange words written

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:01.730
on the wall throughout the movie.

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:05.389
We know they are not English, and likely they
are the same language that Joan made Annie

00:10:05.389 --> 00:10:06.920
recite the ritual spell in.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.690
Here are the four words that I noticed.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:12.820
I couldn’t find much info on Satony other
than the fact that it’s one of the words

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:16.199
used to summon a demon and sounds kind of
similar to Satan.

00:10:16.199 --> 00:10:20.779
Zazas is similar to Zaza or Zozo, which is
part of a supposed phenomenon among Ouija

00:10:20.779 --> 00:10:25.699
board users where, upon asking who they are
speaking to, board would spell out Z-A-Z-A

00:10:25.699 --> 00:10:27.029
or Z-O-Z-O.

00:10:27.029 --> 00:10:30.949
I was only able to find a couple sources online
talking about Liftoach, but I guess it’s

00:10:30.949 --> 00:10:35.209
a rough English spelling of a Hebrew word,
לפתוח , which means open, and it was

00:10:35.209 --> 00:10:42.540
used in this one blackmetal song called Dissection
by Reinkaos where the full line translated

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:45.050
to “blind dragon, open your eyes.”

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:48.209
Could have something to do with those pictures
of Peter with his eyes crossed out.

00:10:48.209 --> 00:10:52.290
Then the last one is Pandemonium, an english
word meaning wild and noisy disorder, and

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:54.740
it also contains the word “demon” inside
of it.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:59.193
Alright, there was a lot to take in with this
movie, so drop me a comment and let me know

00:10:59.193 --> 00:11:01.240
what you noticed, and if you enjoyed the movie,
let me know by giving this video a like.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:05.630
This has been a crazy week if you’re a horror
fan.

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:09.100
New movies, new trailers -- just yesterday
I put out 28 Things You Missed In The Halloween

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.589
Trailer, so be sure to check that out if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:11:11.589 --> 00:11:15.500
I’m gonna be keeping you up to date on all
the Things You Missed, so remember to subscribe

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:21.279
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring
that deathbell for notifications and I’ll

00:11:21.279 --> 00:11:22.769
see you in the next one.

00:11:22.769 --> 00:11:24.920
Assuming, we both survive.

